      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "User-level adoption state leaks into every project",
      "description": "`readAdoptionState` uses `ConfigManager.get()`, which falls back to the user config when the project config has no value. Because `cf config set adoption.state ... --global` is allowed, a global `declined` or `complete` value suppresses brownfield detection in every project without a project-local state; global `in_progress` forces adoption prompts across them. This conflicts with adoption state being repository-owned. Read only the project-scoped value for this state, or otherwise prevent user-level values from influencing it, and add a test covering two projects with a global value.",
